  "label": "The bulldog's confused expression is mapped as 'the most confusing moments'",
  "description": "The text 'the most confusing moments' is overlaid on the image of the bulldog, which is visually interpreted as expressing confusion. This creates an analogical mapping where the bulldog's expression (a visual entity) is mapped onto the concept of 'confusing moments' (a textual entity). The humor arises from anthropomorphizing the dog's expression to represent a human emotional state, creating a direct visual-textual correspondence. The bulldog serves as a visual metaphor for human confusion, and the text explicitly labels this metaphor.",
